msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

msgid "Mereological (part–whole) PHYSICAL containment, not chronological or stratigraphic: a Special Find reused inside a wall, tile fragments inside a reconstructed roof (DP-36). Containment is a relationship, not a change in node type: a US that contains elements is still a US, and the presence of is\\_part\\_of edges is the only discriminant that identifies it as a container. This is the NESTING axis — one primary parent, drawn as a box around its members — so a FunctionalUnitNodeGroup is NOT a target here (its membership is the m:n tag axis is\\_in\\_functional\\_unit, DP-72). A Functional Unit may however be a SOURCE: a whole component physically embedded in a stratigraphic unit (a column engaged in a later wall)."
msgstr ""

